2026-11-01T00:00:00Z (RFD66606-2435) 'a garment is repaired as a distance-field surface
 # uuid: 78ca1f47-05d6-5f1a-a098-56f2945d67ba
 # tags: rfd:title, rfd:flight-level:l1
 RFD:Discussion  1 RFD
 Serials:VSekaiFabric

2026-11-01T00:00:01Z (RFD66606-2435) 'a garment that crosses itself starts the cloth-fit solve as one clean surface.
 # tags: rfd:feature, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2435  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-2435) 'the proxy garment that the cloth-fit solve fits, and how its result returns.
 # tags: rfd:scope, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2435  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2435) 'Can a garment that crosses itself start the cloth-fit solve clean?
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2435  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2435) 'The pants cross themselves 1316 times across 53 shells. The solver takes one connected manifold mesh with no crossings, and a union of those shells did not give one. A surface of the garment's distance field might.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2435  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2435) 'Count the crossing pairs and the shells of the proxy. The solve takes it when they read 0 and 1, and a planted second shell must read 2.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2435  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2435) 'a garment is repaired as a distance-field surface
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2435  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2435) '- The garment is repaired as a proxy. The original keeps its UVs, skin weights and materials.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2435  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2435) '- The proxy is a level surface of the unsigned distance to the garment. Open edges close and layers closer than the distance merge (operator, 2026-11-01).
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2435  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2435) '- The proxy takes skin weights from the garment through the robust weight transfer guest. The fitted displacement returns to the original through the cage stage.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2435  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2435) '- The repair uses no CoACD hulls and no CSG union of the shells (operator, 2026-11-01).
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2435  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2435) '- RFD66606-2424, where a sketch is placed on the avatar before any fit.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2435  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2435) 'What the solver takes
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2435  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2435) 'The cloth-fit solver's input spec asks for an avatar of one or more closed surfaces, because the avatar becomes a signed distance field. It asks for a garment that is a connected manifold triangle mesh. The solver also refuses a start where the garment crosses itself.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2435  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2435) 'The solver's own example solves. Its garment is one shell with no non-manifold edge, 144 open edges (a hem and a waist) and 0 crossing pairs. Its avatar is 32 shells that cross each other 1394 times between shells. So the body may overlap itself, and the garment may not.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2435  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2435) 'What an outfit piece looks like
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2435  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-2435) 'Measured with a throwaway script that welds at one hundred-thousandth of the bounding box and tests each edge against each triangle that shares no vertex. A planted crossing reads 1 and a planted separate pair reads 0.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2435  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-2435) '- The pants have 53 shells, no non-manifold edge, 399 open edges and 1316 crossing pairs. Of those, 1300 are between shells and 16 are inside one shell.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2435  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-2435) '- The skirt has 43 shells and 12 open loops.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2435  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-2435) '- The kimono has 346 shells, 128 open loops and 77 non-manifold edges.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2435  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-2435) '- The pants have 982 vertices that sit twice at one position, and no triangle collapses.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2435  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-2435) 'What did not work
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2435  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-2435) 'A union of the shells did not give a clean surface. Each shell became a solid: an inner copy offset along the vertex normals, joined to the shell by a strip on every open edge. A stock CSG union then ran on all 53 solids.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2435  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:23Z (RFD66606-2435) '- At 4 mm, about five credit cards stacked, 24 of the 53 solids came out inside out, because the small shells are thinner than the offset.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2435  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-2435) '- At 1 mm, about one credit card, all solids were valid. The union still had 295 non-manifold edges and 30969 crossing pairs, against 1316 before.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2435  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-2435) 'Convex hulls from CoACD are closed and cover the garment, but the operator ruled them out for the repair. The pants gave 9 hulls in 6 seconds.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2435  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-2435) 'The distance field
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2435  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:27Z (RFD66606-2435) 'MuJoCo's mesh compiler builds an octree of signed distances. It finds the closest triangle through a bounding-volume hierarchy. It takes the sign from the angle-weighted pseudonormal of the closest vertex, edge or face, so it casts no rays and counts no windings. MuJoCo's GPU port only evaluates that field.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2435  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:28Z (RFD66606-2435) 'The proxy uses the unsigned distance, so the sign never decides the surface. A level surface of it wraps every open edge and cannot cross itself. The distance is an argument that the operator picks. The solver's contact distance is 2 mm, about three credit cards stacked.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2435  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:29Z (RFD66606-2435) 'Rigging and carrying back
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2435  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:30Z (RFD66606-2435) 'The robust weight transfer guest takes the garment as source and the proxy as target. Its arrays are bone-major. It builds its Laplacian with intrinsic mollification (operator, 2026-11-01). With two vertices at one position, a plain cotangent Laplacian gave non-finite weights for 480 of 484 outputs on a test grid, and the mollified one stayed finite.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2435  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:31Z (RFD66606-2435) 'The cage stage binds the original to a cage and moves it with the fitted proxy. That gives a smooth field. Copying the nearest vertex's displacement does not.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2435  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:32Z (RFD66606-2435) 'What is not known
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2435  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:33Z (RFD66606-2435) '- Whether a level surface at the contact distance keeps the garment's folds.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2435  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:34Z (RFD66606-2435) '- Whether it is one shell. The first step counts shells on the pants.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2435  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:35Z (RFD66606-2435) '- Whether the solver takes a garment of several shells. That needs the solver build on the Windows desk.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2435  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:36Z (RFD66606-2435) '- Whether the garments wind consistently. The unsigned field does not need it.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2435  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-01T00:00:37Z (RFD66606-2435) '- Where the nearest-triangle query runs as a guest, and its speed on a 54000-vertex piece.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2435  1 LINE
 Text:Written
